                <pb facs="0153" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg65"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan reports the acceptance by the Chilean Government of an arbitration to be
                    held in Washington. It proposes that one arbitrator be named by the President of
                    each country, and that the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court of the United
                    States will decide all differences between the two arbitrators. Mr. Egan thinks
                    that if the proposition is not satisfactory, the Chilean Government will agree
                    to have the President of one of the Republics in Europe designate a third
                    arbitrator.</p>
            </div>
